name w1-08-degraded-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN W1, SORTIE 8 OF 10 - THE FLIGHT WITH ONE RADAR, RUNG 8 OF THE LADDER.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w1-red-flag.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w1-07-emcon.fbm, and this pair is ONE TOKEN apart - `rf8blu1` carries `set fcr_mode crm`
# (plus the `fcr_range_nm` line that scope range needs) where w1-07's lead carries `off`. Every other
# line of both files, both aggressors included, is identical modulo the callsign prefix.
#
# THE ARENA is w1-01's lane at full length (93.9 km, `--elev const`, 0 m range floor). The one degree of
# freedom this rung adds over rung 7: the sensor asymmetry moves INSIDE the flight.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: is a jet with no radar of its own still a shooter on the flight's shared
# picture, or only a passenger?
#
# C21 IS STILL OPEN AND THIS FILE SAYS WHAT IT FAKES. A real battle-damaged start cannot be declared -
# there is no `.fbm` syntax for initial damage and no repair model to carry it (doc/missions/campaign.md
# section 3) - so a switched-off radar stands in for a shot-out one. The two are not the same thing: a
# failed APG-68 would also cost the fire-control block that `modules/f16/FBF16FireControl` publishes off
# it, while a switched-off one leaves every other box healthy. The substitution's DIRECTION is therefore
# generous to Blue, and a result in which the blind wingman still cannot shoot says something stronger
# than the degraded case would.
#
# WHAT THE TREE ALREADY PREDICTS, so that the run is a test and not a discovery: W5 measured that
# `pilot/FBFlightPicture::Assign` matches every member against the COMPUTING aircraft's own contact list,
# and doc/missions/combat.md says the engagement machine's picture is the Radar block. If both hold, a
# radar-less wingman receives its mate's PPLI, sorts on it, and still has nothing its own trigger will
# fire at. The measurement is `flt_assign` non-zero with `eng_shot_s` = -1 on the same jet.
#
# THE GROUND: `nvbnk8`, a bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind]. Campaign rule 3; not attacked.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, campaign step 8 AND standalone - fingerprint 900fbe8e4af71bf8, identical):
# exit 3. THE RADAR-LESS WINGMAN IS A PASSENGER, AND IT IS WORSE THAN PREDICTED.
#   `rf8blu2`    `fcr_contacts` max **0**, `dl_tracks` max **1** (it HAS its mate's report), `flt_mates`
#                1, `dl_on` 1 - and `flt_assign` max **0**. It is never assigned a target at all, so the
#                predicted signature (an assignment with no shot) is not what happens: the sort has
#                nothing to assign, because `pilot/FBFlightPicture::Assign` matches every member against
#                the COMPUTING aircraft's own contact list (W5's finding 3). `eng_state` `search` 5,807 /
#                `defend` 193, `eng_shots` **0**
#   `rf8blu1`    `fcr_contacts` max 2, `flt_assign` max 2, ONE AIM-120 at t = 128.1 s -> **4.740 m** on
#                `rf8agr1`, degraded, no kill
#   the answer   ONE TOKEN turns a flight that never fires (w1-07: 0 shots, 10 rounds taken) into a flight
#                that fires ONCE. The blind half contributes nothing either way
#   the aggressors' answer an R-27R at **13.513 m** against a **13.8 m** fuze on `rf8blu1` - inside the
#                fuze ring and not a kill, the third such arrival in this campaign
# SO: A JET WITH NO RADAR OF ITS OWN IS NOT A SHOOTER ON THE FLIGHT'S SHARED PICTURE. It receives the
# picture (one datalink track, all run) and is never given a target. What C21 would have added - a
# radar shot to pieces rather than switched off - would have taken the fire-control block with it and
# made the answer more negative, not less.
#
# WHAT TO READ: on `rf8blu2` (the blind one) `flt_src` / `flt_assign` / `eng_state` / `eng_shot_s`
# together - a jet with an assignment and no shot is a passenger, and the two columns say which; then the
# same block on `rf8blu1` and the diff of the whole run against w1-07.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected shape; exit 1 means a Blue jet was lost. The verdict is
# the pair (`flt_assign` on the blind wingman, its `eng_shot_s`) read beside w1-07's all-blind pair.
# exit 2 would be a defect.

unit rf8blu1
  team friendly
  flight blu8 1
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on                             # the flight keeps its cooperative net
  set fcr_mode crm                            # THE ONE TOKEN: w1-07's lead had `off` here
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit rf8blu2
  team friendly
  flight blu8 2
  module f16
  spawn 37.28198 -115.52000 8150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.28198 -116.58000 8150 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit rf8agr1
  team hostile
  flight agr8 1
  module mig29
  spawn 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission off                       # the documented power-up state, O2's policy
  set kols_mode ir                            # the passive primary sensor, powered and publishing
  set kols_laser on                           # ...and armed, so a tracked source inside 6 km gets a range
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 90 90 8                    # the controller's three BRAA calls: bearing, range in km,
  set brief_gci 60 90 60 8                    # target altitude in km - typed, one entry per decision
  set brief_gci 100 90 40 8                   # tick, refusable by the bus like any other input
  wp 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit rf8agr2
  team hostile
  flight agr8 2
  module mig29
  spawn 37.31802 -116.58000 8150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission off
  set kols_mode ir
  set kols_laser on
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 90 90 8
  set brief_gci 60 90 60 8
  set brief_gci 100 90 40 8
  wp 37.31802 -115.52000 8150 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit nvbnk8
  module target_hard                          # bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind]
  team hostile
  spawn 37.30000 -116.20000 ground 90.0 0
